      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the pointer to MutableEntry!\n\nThe difference is the ownership scope:\n\n- EntriesIterator holds its own MutableEntry per iterator instance, so each thread gets its own copy.\n\n- PackOffset result is a field of MultiPackIndexV1 itself — a singleton per repository — so every concurrent find() writes to the same object. Same for OffsetCalculator.mutablePo.\n\nThere is no per-call scope for find()/decode() like there is for iterator(), so allocating a fresh PackOffset per call is the most straightforward fix. PackOffset is just two primitives (int + long), so the allocation cost should be negligible.",
      "parentUuid": "ca34ac62_61a97a66",
